            {
              "type": "frame",
              "id": "FjFyG",
              "name": "Messages",
              "clip": true,
              "width": "fill_container",
              "height": "fill_container",
              "layout": "vertical",
              "gap": "$n:spacing-md",
              "padding": "$n:spacing-sm",
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "UZzAk",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "n:i5vQ3i",
                  "name": "AI Message",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "n:FHA10": {
                      "content": "...discretionary spending conversation while their retirement savings rate is at 8%, their emergency fund has $3,000 in it, and they're hoping to \"catch up later.\"",
                      "fill": "$n:sem-chatTextPrimary",
                      "lineHeight": 1.6
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "A49E4n",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "n:i5vQ3i",
                  "name": "AI Message",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "n:FHA10": {
                      "content": "If you want, I can run the numbers specific to your situation — your age, income, current savings — to see where you actually stand and whether that upgrade fits into your plan.",
                      "fill": "$n:sem-chatTextPrimary",
                      "lineHeight": 1.6
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "type": "frame",
                  "id": "LdKLN",
                  "name": "User Bubble Wrap",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "justifyContent": "end",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "type": "frame",
                      "id": "tCDBf",
                      "name": "User Bubble",
                      "fill": "$n:sem-chatBubbleUser",
                      "cornerRadius": [
                        "$n:radius-xs",
                        "$n:radius-xs",
                        "$n:radius-4xs",
                        "$n:radius-xs"
                      ],
                      "layout": "vertical",
                      "padding": "$n:spacing-sm",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "type": "text",
                          "id": "oO6DS",
                          "name": "User Text",
                          "fill": "$n:sem-chatTextPrimary",
                          "content": "but i am worried about buying a\nused car that may have issues and\nwill also cost me a pretty penny",
                          "lineHeight": 1.6,
                          "fontFamily": "$n:typo-primary-base-regular-font-family",
                          "fontSize": "$n:typo-primary-base-regular-font-size",
                          "fontWeight": "normal"
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "id": "J1LBP2",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "n:i5vQ3i",
                  "name": "AI Message",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "n:FHA10": {
                      "content": "That's a legitimate concern — but it's also the exact fear that dealerships leverage to upsell you into expensive leases or new car purchases. Let me break down the real math and risks.",
                      "fill": "$n:sem-chatTextPrimary",
                      "lineHeight": 1.6
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "BewLL",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "n:i5vQ3i",
                  "name": "AI Message",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "n:FHA10": {
                      "content": "The math is clear: even in a worst-case repair scenario, you come out tens of thousands of dollars ahead by buying used. The \"risk\" of repairs is real but manageable; the certainty of overpaying $30,000+ for a lease is guaranteed.",
                      "fill": "$n:sem-chatTextPrimary",
                      "lineHeight": 1.6
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "vxIU5",
                  "type": "ref",
                  "ref": "n:i5vQ3i",
                  "name": "AI Message",
                  "width": "fill_container",
                  "descendants": {
                    "n:FHA10": {
                      "content": "The smart play: buy a 3-5 year old CPO from a reliable brand, get a pre-purchase inspection, set aside $100-150/month for repairs, and invest the difference. If you're truly worried about catastrophic repair risk, spend $2,000 on an extended warranty — you're still $26,000 ahead of the lease.",
                      "fill": "$n:sem-chatTextPrimary",
                      "lineHeight": 1.6
                    }
                  }
                }
              ]
            },
